        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  DANCE — LANDSCAPE MAP                           |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  WESTERN THEATRICAL DANCE                                        |\n|  Ballet: court origins (1489+) → Romantic (1832) → Petipa       |\n|          (1870-1903) → Balanchine neoclassicism → contemporary  |\n|                                                                  |\n|  Modern Dance: Duncan (1900s) → Graham (1920s+) →               |\n|    Cunningham (1950s+) → Release technique → Post-Judson        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  Postmodern Dance: Judson Dance Theater (1962+)                  |\n|    → Steve Paxton (contact improv) → Pina Bausch (Tanztheater)  |\n|                                                                  |\n|  NON-WESTERN CLASSICAL FORMS                                     |\n|  Kathak (North India): ghungroo bells, footwork, spins          |\n|  Bharatanatyam (South India): geometric, sculptural, mudra       |\n|  Kathakali (Kerala): drama + extreme codified movement          |\n|  Noh movement (Japan): extreme slowness, weight, ma (interval)  |\n|  Beijing Opera movement (China): acrobatics + symbolic gesture  |\n|                                                                  |\n|  SOCIAL AND FOLK DANCE                                           |\n|  (not covered here — vast; each culture, many forms)            |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
