        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nBALLET ORIGINS (1489-1670)\n---------------------------\nBegan not as theater but as court entertainment:\n  1489: Bergamo, Italy — elaborate banquet entertainment\n    with \"dances\" between courses representing themes.\n  Ballo: Italian for \"ball game\" or \"dance.\"\n  Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx: Ballet Comique de la Reine (1581,\n    Paris) — considered the first \"ballet\" as a whole event\n    (5.5 hours; court performance)."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DANCE.md#008",
      "path": [
        "08-DANCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:theater-performance:08-dance, git-history:theater-performance:08-dance]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
        "concepts": "[dance]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:dance",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[dance]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Early ballet = spectacle for the court nobility:\n    The AUDIENCE was also sometimes the PERFORMERS\n    (noble guests danced in the interludes).\n    Louis XIV (Sun King) was an avid dancer and\n    performed in court ballets into his mid-20s.\n    He founded the Academie Royale de Danse in 1661 —\n    the first formal dance institution in the West."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DANCE.md#009",
      "path": [
        "08-DANCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:theater-performance:08-dance, git-history:theater-performance:08-dance]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
        "concepts": "[dance]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:dance",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[dance]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The classical ballet vocabulary (five positions,\n  turned-out legs, the technical terms) was codified\n  by the French court ballet tradition.\n  Raoul Auger Feuillet published Choregraphie (1700) —\n  the first notation system for ballet.\n```"
    },
