        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[dance]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TECHNOLOGIES THAT ENABLED IT:\n  Pointe technique (dancing on the tips of the toes):\n    Made possible by a reinforced tip in the slipper.\n    Creates the appearance of weightlessness, ethereality.\n    Marie Taglioni is credited with the first significant\n    use of pointe work (La Sylphide, 1832).\n  Gas lighting: enabled atmospheric effects (moonlight,\n    forest at night) that the Romantic aesthetic required."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DANCE.md#014",
      "path": [
        "08-DANCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:theater-performance:08-dance, git-history:theater-performance:08-dance]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
