        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[dance]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY WORKS:\n  La Sylphide (1832): a Scottish man loves a supernatural\n    sylph; when he catches her, she dies. First Romantic ballet.\n  Giselle (1841): peasant girl dies of a broken heart;\n    returns as a wili (spirit of a betrayed maiden);\n    saves the man who broke her heart from the other wilis.\n    Still performed; the ultimate Romantic ballet.\n```"
    },
    {
