      "text": "```\nMARIUS PETIPA (1818-1910)\n--------------------------\nFrench-born, worked in Russia 1847-1903.\nThe most influential choreographer in ballet history.\nFormalized the \"classical ballet\" we know today."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DANCE.md#017",
      "path": [
        "08-DANCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:theater-performance:08-dance, git-history:theater-performance:08-dance]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
        "concepts": "[dance]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/08-DANCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:dance",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[dance]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY STRUCTURES Petipa established:\n1. The Grand Pas de Deux\n   The centerpiece of classical ballet:\n   - Adagio: ballerina and partner in supported turns,\n             lifts, balances. Slow, expansive, display of\n             line and partnership.\n   - Male Variation: the male dancer's solo.\n             Technical display: jumps, turns.\n   - Female Variation: the ballerina's solo.\n             Pointe work, turns, balances.\n   - Coda: both together; virtuosic finale.\n             Repeated pirouettes, jumps, chaîné turns."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DANCE.md#018",
      "path": [
        "08-DANCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:theater-performance:08-dance, git-history:theater-performance:08-dance]",
